From: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: qcom ppe: do not double-disable NAPI on delete

napi_disable() on a NAPI that is already disabled (or never enabled) waits
forever. edma_cfg_{rx,tx}_napi_delete() called it unconditionally, so any
probe error (or module removal) after the NAPI was created hung in
napi_disable_locked() with RTNL held, blocking the rest of the boot.

Signed-off-by: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_tx.c
@@ -633,7 +633,12 @@
 		if (!txcmpl_ring->napi_added)
 			continue;
 
-		napi_disable(&txcmpl_ring->napi);
+		/* NAPI is created disabled and edma_cfg_tx_napi_disable() may
+		 * already have run: a second napi_disable() would then wait
+		 * forever (NAPI_STATE_SCHED never clears).
+		 */
+		if (!test_bit(NAPI_STATE_SCHED, &txcmpl_ring->napi.state))
+			napi_disable(&txcmpl_ring->napi);
 		netif_napi_del(&txcmpl_ring->napi);
 		txcmpl_ring->napi_added = false;
 	}
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
@@ -922,7 +922,8 @@
 		if (!rxdesc_ring->napi_added)
 			continue;
 
-		napi_disable(&rxdesc_ring->napi);
+		if (!test_bit(NAPI_STATE_SCHED, &rxdesc_ring->napi.state))
+			napi_disable(&rxdesc_ring->napi);
 		netif_napi_del(&rxdesc_ring->napi);
 		rxdesc_ring->napi_added = false;
 	}
